{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/electrolysis-calculations/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/electrolysis-calculations.html","area":"students","kind":"topic","title":"Electrolysis Calculations - Chemistry","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<!-- Header -->\n    <nav class=\"bg-white shadow-sm fixed top-0 w-full z-50\">\n        <div class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4\">\n            <div class=\"flex justify-between h-16 items-center\">\n                <div class=\"flex items-center\">\n                    <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/\" class=\"text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 mr-4\">\n                        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>\n                    </a>\n                    <h1 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900\">Electrolysis Calculations</h1>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"flex items-center space-x-4\">\n                    <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 hidden sm:block\">\n                        Progress: <span id=\"progressPercent\">0%</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"w-24 sm:w-32 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full\">\n                        <div id=\"progressBar\" class=\"h-2 bg-indigo-500 rounded-full transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </nav>\n\n    <!-- Main Content -->\n    <main class=\"pt-20 pb-8 px-4 max-w-5xl mx-auto\">\n        <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n        <div class=\"bg-indigo-50 border-l-4 border-indigo-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6 animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-indigo-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Calculate the charge transferred using Q = I × t</li>\n                <li>• Use Faraday's constant to calculate moles of electrons</li>\n                <li>• Calculate mass of products formed during electrolysis</li>\n                <li>• Calculate volume of gases produced at electrodes</li>\n                <li>• Apply Faraday's laws of electrolysis to problems</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 1: Basic Concepts -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n                Key Equations and Constants\n            </h2>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-blue-500 mb-4\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bolt mr-2\" data-mi=\"bolt\">bolt</span>Charge Equation</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">The total charge transferred during electrolysis is:</p>\n                <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg text-center text-xl font-mono\">\n                    <strong>Q = I × t</strong>\n                </div>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-2\">Where: Q = charge (Coulombs), I = current (Amperes), t = time (seconds)</p>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-purple-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-700 mb-2 text-center\">Faraday's Constant</h4>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg text-center\">\n                        <p class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-purple-600\">F = 96,500 C/mol</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-2 text-center\">The charge carried by 1 mole of electrons</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 mb-2 text-center\">Molar Gas Volume</h4>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg text-center\">\n                        <p class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-green-600\">Vm = 24 dm³/mol</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-2 text-center\">Volume of 1 mole of gas at RTP (25°C, 1 atm)</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-amber-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-amber-500\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Key Relationship</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Moles of electrons = Q / F = (I × t) / 96,500</p>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\">This is the foundation for all electrolysis calculations!</p>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 2: Faraday's Laws -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n                Faraday's Laws of Electrolysis\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-rose-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-rose-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-rose-700 mb-2\">First Law</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">The mass of substance deposited/dissolved is <strong>directly proportional</strong> to the quantity of electricity passed.</p>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                        <p class=\"text-center font-mono\">m ∝ Q</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-center font-mono mt-1\">m = (I × t × Ar) / (n × F)</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-xs mt-2\">n = number of electrons transferred per ion</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-teal-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-teal-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-teal-700 mb-2\">Second Law</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\">The masses of different substances deposited by the same quantity of electricity are proportional to their <strong>equivalent weights</strong>.</p>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                        <p class=\"text-center font-mono\">m ∝ M/n</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-center font-mono mt-1\">Equivalent weight = Ar / n</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-xs mt-2\">M = molar mass, n = charge on ion</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -list-ol mr-2\" data-mi=\"format_list_numbered\">format_list_numbered</span>Common Ion Charges</h4>\n                <div class=\"grid grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-6 gap-2 text-sm\">\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\">\n                        <p class=\"font-medium\">Ag⁺</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">n = 1</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\">\n                        <p class=\"font-medium\">Cu⁺</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">n = 1</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\">\n                        <p class=\"font-medium\">Cu²⁺</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">n = 2</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\">\n                        <p class=\"font-medium\">Pb²⁺</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">n = 2</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\">\n                        <p class=\"font-medium\">Al³⁺</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">n = 3</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\">\n                        <p class=\"font-medium\">Fe³⁺</p>\n                        <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">n = 3</p>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 3: Step-by-Step Method -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n                Step-by-Step Calculation Method\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-green-500 mb-4\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -list-check mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>General Steps</h4>\n                <ol class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm space-y-2\">\n                    <li><span class=\"bg-green-200 text-green-800 w-6 h-6 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center text-xs mr-2 font-bold\">1</span>Write the balanced half-equation</li>\n                    <li><span class=\"bg-green-200 text-green-800 w-6 h-6 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center text-xs mr-2 font-bold\">2</span>Calculate charge: Q = I × t</li>\n                    <li><span class=\"bg-green-200 text-green-800 w-6 h-6 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center text-xs mr-2 font-bold\">3</span>Calculate moles of electrons: moles e⁻ = Q / F</li>\n                    <li><span class=\"bg-green-200 text-green-800 w-6 h-6 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center text-xs mr-2 font-bold\">4</span>Use the mole ratio from half-equation</li>\n                    <li><span class=\"bg-green-200 text-green-800 w-6 h-6 rounded-full inline-flex items-center justify-center text-xs mr-2 font-bold\">5</span>Calculate mass or volume as required</li>\n                </ol>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -weight-hanging mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>For Mass</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Mass = moles × Mr</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-purple-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -wind mr-2\" data-mi=\"air\">air</span>For Gas Volume</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Volume = moles × 24 dm³ (at RTP)</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 4: Worked Example 1 -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n                Worked Example: Calculating Mass\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-amber-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-amber-200 mb-4\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-700 mb-2\">Problem</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-700\">Calculate the mass of copper deposited when a current of 2.5 A flows through CuSO₄ solution for 30 minutes.</p>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Write the half-equation</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-blue-600 font-mono\">Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-sm\">Ratio: 2 mol e⁻ : 1 mol Cu</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Calculate charge</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Q = I × t = 2.5 A × (30 × 60) s</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Q = 2.5 × 1800 = <strong>4500 C</strong></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Calculate moles of electrons</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Moles e⁻ = Q / F = 4500 / 96500</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Moles e⁻ = <strong>0.0466 mol</strong></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Step 4:</strong> Calculate moles of Cu</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">From half-equation: 2 mol e⁻ → 1 mol Cu</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Moles Cu = 0.0466 / 2 = <strong>0.0233 mol</strong></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-green-700 mb-2\"><strong>Step 5:</strong> Calculate mass</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Mass Cu = moles × Ar = 0.0233 × 63.5</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-green-700 font-bold text-lg\">Mass Cu = 1.48 g</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 5: Worked Example 2 -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n                Worked Example: Calculating Gas Volume\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-amber-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-amber-200 mb-4\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-700 mb-2\">Problem</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-700\">Calculate the volume of oxygen produced at the anode when a current of 0.5 A flows through dilute H₂SO₄ for 1 hour.</p>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Write the half-equation</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-blue-600 font-mono\">4OH⁻ → O₂ + 2H₂O + 4e⁻</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-sm\">Ratio: 4 mol e⁻ : 1 mol O₂</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Calculate charge</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Q = I × t = 0.5 A × (1 × 60 × 60) s</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Q = 0.5 × 3600 = <strong>1800 C</strong></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Calculate moles of electrons</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Moles e⁻ = Q / F = 1800 / 96500</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Moles e⁻ = <strong>0.0187 mol</strong></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Step 4:</strong> Calculate moles of O₂</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">From half-equation: 4 mol e⁻ → 1 mol O₂</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Moles O₂ = 0.0187 / 4 = <strong>0.00467 mol</strong></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-green-700 mb-2\"><strong>Step 5:</strong> Calculate volume</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Volume O₂ = moles × 24 dm³</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Volume O₂ = 0.00467 × 24</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-green-700 font-bold text-lg\">Volume O₂ = 0.112 dm³ = 112 cm³</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 6: Worked Example 3 -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">6</span>\n                Worked Example: Finding Current or Time\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-amber-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-amber-200 mb-4\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-700 mb-2\">Problem</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-700\">What current is needed to deposit 5.4 g of silver from AgNO₃ solution in 2 hours?</p>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Write the half-equation</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-blue-600 font-mono\">Ag⁺ + e⁻ → Ag</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-sm\">Ratio: 1 mol e⁻ : 1 mol Ag</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Calculate moles of Ag</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Moles Ag = mass / Ar = 5.4 / 108</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Moles Ag = <strong>0.05 mol</strong></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Calculate moles of electrons</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">From half-equation: 1 mol Ag requires 1 mol e⁻</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Moles e⁻ = <strong>0.05 mol</strong></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Step 4:</strong> Calculate charge</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Q = moles e⁻ × F = 0.05 × 96500</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Q = <strong>4825 C</strong></p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-green-700 mb-2\"><strong>Step 5:</strong> Calculate current</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Q = I × t → I = Q / t</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">t = 2 hours = 2 × 60 × 60 = 7200 s</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600\">I = 4825 / 7200</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-green-700 font-bold text-lg\">I = 0.67 A</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 7: Video -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">7</span>\n                Video: Electrolysis Calculations\n            </h2>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n                <div class=\"video-container\">\n                    <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/PmNiE5qCmiU\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 8: Practice Problems -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-indigo-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n                Practice Questions\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. Calculate the mass of lead deposited when a current of 3 A flows through molten PbBr₂ for 1 hour.</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            <strong>Half-equation:</strong> Pb²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Pb (2 mol e⁻ : 1 mol Pb)<br>\n                            <strong>Q = I × t = 3 × 3600 = 10,800 C</strong><br>\n                            <strong>Moles e⁻ = 10800/96500 = 0.112 mol</strong><br>\n                            <strong>Moles Pb = 0.112/2 = 0.056 mol</strong><br>\n                            <strong>Mass Pb = 0.056 × 207 = 11.6 g</strong>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. What volume of hydrogen gas (at RTP) is produced at the cathode when a current of 5 A passes through dilute H₂SO₄ for 20 minutes?</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            <strong>Half-equation:</strong> 2H⁺ + 2e⁻ → H₂ (2 mol e⁻ : 1 mol H₂)<br>\n                            <strong>Q = I × t = 5 × (20 × 60) = 6000 C</strong><br>\n                            <strong>Moles e⁻ = 6000/96500 = 0.0622 mol</strong><br>\n                            <strong>Moles H₂ = 0.0622/2 = 0.0311 mol</strong><br>\n                            <strong>Volume H₂ = 0.0311 × 24 = 0.746 dm³ = 746 cm³</strong>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. How long must a current of 2 A flow to deposit 3.18 g of copper from CuSO₄ solution?</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            <strong>Half-equation:</strong> Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu (2 mol e⁻ : 1 mol Cu)<br>\n                            <strong>Moles Cu = 3.18/63.5 = 0.05 mol</strong><br>\n                            <strong>Moles e⁻ = 0.05 × 2 = 0.1 mol</strong><br>\n                            <strong>Q = 0.1 × 96500 = 9650 C</strong><br>\n                            <strong>t = Q/I = 9650/2 = 4825 s = 80.4 min = 1 hour 20 min</strong>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">4. A current of 1.5 A flows through AgNO₃ solution. Calculate the mass of silver deposited in 45 minutes.</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            <strong>Half-equation:</strong> Ag⁺ + e⁻ → Ag (1 mol e⁻ : 1 mol Ag)<br>\n                            <strong>Q = I × t = 1.5 × (45 × 60) = 4050 C</strong><br>\n                            <strong>Moles e⁻ = 4050/96500 = 0.042 mol</strong><br>\n                            <strong>Moles Ag = 0.042 mol (same ratio)</strong><br>\n                            <strong>Mass Ag = 0.042 × 108 = 4.54 g</strong>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-indigo-50 to-purple-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-indigo-200 animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-indigo-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-indigo-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n                <li>• Q = I × t (charge = current × time in seconds)</li>\n                <li>• Moles of electrons = Q / 96,500 (Faraday's constant)</li>\n                <li>• Always write the half-equation to find the mole ratio</li>\n                <li>• Mass = moles × Mr; Gas volume = moles × 24 dm³</li>\n                <li>• The number of electrons (n) equals the ion charge</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Navigation -->\n        <div class=\"flex justify-between items-center mt-8\">\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/discharge-factors/\" class=\"px-4 py-2 text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-900\">\n                <span class=\"mi -chevron-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"chevron_left\">chevron_left</span>Previous\n            </a>\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/faradays-laws/\" class=\"px-4 py-2 bg-indigo-500 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-indigo-600\">\n                Next: Faraday's Laws<span class=\"mi -chevron-right ml-2\" data-mi=\"chevron_right\">chevron_right</span>\n            </a>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    \n\n<!-- Topic Tracking and Quiz System -->\n  \n\n\n<div data-bidemy=\"quiz\"></div>","bodyClass":"bg-gray-50 min-h-screen","bodyStyle":"","css":["@keyframes fade-in-up {\n            from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px); }\n            to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }\n        }\n        .animate-fade-in-up { animation: fade-in-up 0.5s ease-out forwards; }\n        .section-card {\n            background: white;\n            border-radius: 12px;\n            padding: 1.5rem;\n            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;\n            box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);\n            border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;\n        }\n        .video-container {\n            position: relative;\n            width: 100%;\n            padding-bottom: 56.25%;\n            height: 0;\n            overflow: hidden;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            background: #f9fafb;\n        }\n        .video-container iframe {\n            position: absolute;\n            top: 0; left: 0;\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 100%;\n            border: none;\n        }\n        .math-formula {\n            font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\n            font-style: italic;\n        }"],"quiz":{"topicId":"electrolysis-calculations","subject":"chemistry","passingScore":60,"questions":[{"question":"What is the formula for calculating charge in electrolysis?","options":["Q = I / t","Q = I × t","Q = I + t","Q = I - t"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Charge (Q) = Current (I) × Time (t). Time must be in seconds."},{"question":"What is the value of Faraday's constant?","options":["965 C/mol","9650 C/mol","96500 C/mol","965000 C/mol"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Faraday's constant F = 96,500 C/mol, representing the charge carried by 1 mole of electrons."},{"question":"Calculate the charge when 2 A flows for 10 minutes.","options":["20 C","200 C","1200 C","12000 C"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Q = I × t = 2 × (10 × 60) = 2 × 600 = 1200 C"},{"question":"How many moles of electrons are carried by 193,000 C of charge?","options":["0.5 mol","1 mol","2 mol","4 mol"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Moles of electrons = Q/F = 193,000/96,500 = 2 mol"},{"question":"In the half-equation Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu, how many moles of electrons are needed to deposit 1 mol of Cu?","options":["0.5 mol e⁻","1 mol e⁻","2 mol e⁻","4 mol e⁻"],"correct":2,"explanation":"From the equation, 2 moles of electrons are needed to deposit 1 mole of copper."},{"question":"What volume of gas (at RTP) is produced by 0.5 mol of any gas?","options":["12 dm³","24 dm³","48 dm³","0.5 dm³"],"correct":0,"explanation":"At RTP, molar gas volume = 24 dm³/mol. Volume = 0.5 × 24 = 12 dm³"},{"question":"Calculate the mass of Ag deposited by 9650 C. (Ag = 108 g/mol, Ag⁺ + e⁻ → Ag)","options":["0.1 g","1.08 g","10.8 g","108 g"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Moles e⁻ = 9650/96500 = 0.1 mol. Moles Ag = 0.1 mol (1:1 ratio). Mass = 0.1 × 108 = 10.8 g"},{"question":"How long must a 5 A current flow to deposit 3.175 g of Cu? (Cu = 63.5, Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu)","options":["386 s","965 s","1930 s","3860 s"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Moles Cu = 3.175/63.5 = 0.05 mol. Moles e⁻ = 0.1 mol. Q = 0.1 × 96500 = 9650 C. t = 9650/5 = 1930 s"}]},"tracker":{"topicId":"electrolysis-calculations","topicTitle":"Electrolysis Calculations","subject":"chemistry","sections":["section-1","section-2","section-3","section-4","section-5","section-6","section-7","section-8"],"quizRequired":true},"links":[]}